# The kill -9 exit criterion (PRD C5), first run: a composer on the real store backend, a local
# (server-less) account, a character typed through the editor's helper every 200 ms. The
# harness (tools/kill9-compose.sh) reads the log and kills this process with SIGKILL at a
# random moment. Every text is a run of letters; nothing personal.
desktop tiling
resize 1440 900
mail-account Local
composer-backend store
composer-open new
composer-wait
composer-focus body
composer-type-log $TMP/typed.log 200 900
